be 435)\n\n`0.29` has the same problem. All the totals tests failed because of it.\n\n**Fix:** convert through `Decimal(str(amount))` and round half-up to whole cents. Using `str()` means a float like `19.99` is read as the decimal value it was written as, not its binary approximation. Spot checks: `19.99\u21921999`, `4.35\u2192435`, `0.29\u219229`, `-1.15\u2192-115`, `\"2.50\"\u2192250`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- Amounts with fractions of a cent now round half-up (`0.005 \u2192 1`). Before, they were cut off. Negative halves round away from zero (`-0.005 \u2192 -1`), which matches the discount and tax code.\n- Collection fails without `PYTHONPATH=.` because there's no `conftest.py` or pytest config putting the repo root on the path. I left that alone since it's outside the bug.\n- Behind this bug is a design problem: prices come in as floats. Passing prices as strings or `Decimal` would remove this whole class of error; `to_cents` already accepts both.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 107656, "requests_cache_write": 14272, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1267872, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1692, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial23", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 44, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T00:02:45.116285+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.641, "t_checker_s": 0.382, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1706, "tokens_cache_read": 107656, "tokens_cache_write": 14272, "tokens_fresh": 1706, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 107656, 